# THE TRIGGER, MEASURED RATHER THAN COPIED (2026-10-02).
#
# An earlier pass REFUSED to card this one and was right to. It assumed one rigid origin
# delta per export and took it from the bodies -- which are 0.019 units apart, so it then
# found the trigger 2.42 units from where Vanilla's lands and would not guess across that.
#
# The two triggers were then compared directly. Both are 52 verts and 42 tris, and with each
# centred on its own centroid the MAXIMUM PER-VERTEX DIFFERENCE IS 0.000000 -- the same part,
# purely translated, not rotated and not reshaped:
#
#     -2.4219, 0.0000, -0.0938
#
# So Vanilla's hinge for this mesh applies unchanged and only the pivot moves. Its axis and
# its 30.15 degrees are kept; its pivot -21.722, 0, -3.952 is shifted by that delta. The
# surface is called `hidden` here and `trigger` in Vanilla's export, which is why it had to be
# found by geometry -- the name says nothing and the body's own delta actively misleads.
part trigger
  role    = trigger
  surface = hidden
  dof
    kind    = hinge
    axis    = 0, 1, 0
    degrees = 30.15
    pivot   = -24.144, 0.000, -4.046
  end
end

