# AN M16 (owner). An AR-15 charging handle is NON-RECIPROCATING: it sits
# still while the bolt carrier cycles inside the receiver, and an AR has no
# last-round bolt hold-open -- which is exactly why its shooters hit the bolt
# catch by hand.
#
# IT WAS CARDED LIKE A PISTOL: only `role = action`, so SynthCycle gave it the
# defaults it carries for a slide -- holdOpenWhenEmpty and autoOnShot
# (verb.zs:326-344). Right for BD_Pistol, which is a Beretta. Not right here.
#
# `auto = onshotstill` is the key the system already had for this, and verb.zs:124-126
# names a real gun in its comment: the shot does the stroke's bookkeeping -- eject,
# feed, hold-open -- and DRAWS NO MOTION.
#
# BOTH VERBS DECLARED, not just the one being changed: SynthesiseVerbs is
# all-or-nothing (card.zs:918), so one declared verb synthesises NONE. That is how the
# machine gun lost its magazine swap this morning. The numbers are SynthCycle's and
# SynthSwap's own, so nothing but the two intended keys moves.
cycle rack
  part     = charginghandle
  outat    = 0.6
  apex     = 0.95
  onout    = eject
  from     = chamber
  onhome   = feed
  feed     = mag
  into     = chamber
  return   = spring
  auto     = onshotstill
  holdopen = never
end

swap magwell
  part     = magazine
  store    = mag
  detachat = 0.9
  pullout  = 0.97
  button   = yes
  handtake = no
end
